        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Managed budgets up to $5,000 and coordinated 15 events during 12-day festival, overseeing venue logistics, volunteer teams, and guest services</li>
          <li>Collaborated with venue owners, staff, and vendors to execute seamless event experiences for performers and attendees</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-head">
          <h3 class="job-title">Production Coordinator | Gaia Film Festival (Gaiam)</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="job-meta">Louisville, CO | Mar 2008 - July 2008</p>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Led training and coordination for 75+ volunteers, fostering teamwork while managing schedules, ticketing systems, and guest accommodations</li>
          <li>Worked directly with venue partners to deliver high-quality festival experience, managing budgets and sponsor relationships</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-head">
          <h3 class="job-title">Baker Barista | Spruce Confections</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="job-meta">Boulder, CO | Jan 2005 - Feb 2007</p>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Prepared wholesale and retail batches daily, maintaining quality standards and adhering to food safety protocols in fast-paced kitchen environment</li>
          <li>Delivered consistent customer service while managing multiple orders and maintaining clean, organized workspace</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
        <div class="job-head">
          <h3 class="job-title">Assistant Manager | Joe Van Gogh (formerly Joe City Roasters)</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="job-meta">Greensboro, NC | Dec 1994 - Dec 1996</p>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Supported all daily operations including wholesale, retail, and lunch service, ensuring smooth function across multiple service areas</li>
          <li>Increased revenues by implementing gift basket production and maintaining high customer service standards</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div>
          <h2 class="section-title" id="education">Education</h2>
          <div class="section-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="para">Metropolitan State University of Denver — BA, Social Documentary Journalism (2015-2018)</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="section-title" id="tools">Selected Tools</h2>
          <div class="section-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="para">Salesforce | Google Drive | Microsoft Office | WordPress | Event Management Software</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="volunteer">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="volunteer">Volunteer Leadership</h2>
      <div class="section-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <p class="para">Media Mecca Volunteer Co-Coordinator, Burning Man (2018-present)</p>
      <p class="para" style="margin-bottom:0;">Frances Belford Wayne Merit Award recipient</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
